{"step_index":1312,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T14:19:19Z","input_tokens":2372,"cache_read_tokens":253692,"output_tokens":1659,"content":"### Phase 3 Implementation Summary: Add Meaningful Animations\n\n**Phase 3 — Add meaningful animations** has been implemented. All animations are lightweight, organic CSS-driven transitions synchronized directly with the execution engine snapshots. They can be dynamically sped up, slowed down, or completely disabled for reduced-motion accessibility.\n\n---\n\n### Files Changed\n\n1. [app_build/styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css)\n   - **Active Code Line & Branch Highlights**: Added `.code-row.is-current-line` luminous gradient sweep (`lineEntranceHighlight`), pulsating execution pointer (`pointerPulse`), and conditional branch badges (`.branch-badge.is-executes` with `branchGlow` and `.branch-badge.is-skipped`).\n   - **Number Gliding & Variable Box Transitions**: Added `numberGlide` for calculated numbers moving into variable boxes, `arrowGlide` for flow indicators, and `numPopIn` for newly assigned values.\n   - **Variable Creation & Update Animations**: Added `varCreatedGlow` (blue aura) for new variables, `varUpdatedGlow` (emerald aura) for re-assigned variables, and `.var-status-badge` (`+ Created`, `Updated`, `⚠ Negative`).\n   - **Arithmetic Demonstrations**: Added `operandAppear` and `calcResultPop` (spring bounce with green glow) for compound assignments and arithmetic formula evaluations.\n   - **Condition Comparisons & Decisions**: Added `decisionSpring` for `✓ TRUE` and `✗ FALSE` decision badges, and `activeBranchPop` for executing branches.\n   - **Loop Transitions**: Added `loopSpin` for the looping indicator icon (`↺`), `loopBannerSlide` for loop pass banners, `activeCellGlow` for array list cells, and `pointerBounce` for the active list element pointer.\n   - **Negative Reset Visualization**: Added `discardNegative` (strikethrough drop) and `freshZeroPop` (clean zero appearance) when `c < 0` triggers `c = 0`.\n   - **Speed Factor & Reduced-Motion Accessibility**: Scaled all keyframe durations by `var(--anim-speed-factor)`. Added zero-mo\n<truncated 1732 bytes>\nitions** | Looping icon spins (`↺`), loop pass banner slides down, and list array pointer (`▲ pointer`) bounces under `nums[i]`. | 700ms smooth spin (`loopSpin`) and 400ms array cell glow (`activeCellGlow`). |\n| **Negative Discard & Reset** | Discarded negative running total drops with a strikethrough, and a fresh zero pops in. | 500ms discard drop (`discardNegative`) + 450ms fresh start pop (`freshZeroPop`). |\n| **Speed & Motion Controls** | ⚡ Speed cycles `0.5x` (slow/teaching), `1x` (normal), `1.5x` (brisk), `2x` (fast). Reduced Motion toggle instantly removes all animations. | Controlled via CSS variable `--anim-speed-factor`. Automatically respects OS prefers-reduced-motion. |\n| **Strict Engine Sync** | Every animation is purely visual CSS on top of immutable step snapshots. | Moving backward or forward with Previous/Next restores the exact runtime snapshot instantly. |\n\n---\n\n### Verification & Automated Test Results\n\nThe suite was validated using automated Node.js execution against all 5 test presets, while loops, and class mutations:\n\n```text\nChecking engine and explainer integrity...\n[PASS] Mixed (Original Kadane):  expected 6, got 6, total steps: 54\n[PASS] All-Negative (Kadane):    expected -1, got -1, total steps: 39\n[PASS] All-Positive (Kadane):    expected 15, got 15, total steps: 36\n[PASS] Single Negative (Kadane): expected -7, got -7, total steps: 17\n[PASS] Single Positive (Kadane): expected 42, got 42, total steps: 16\n[PASS] Binary Search:            expected 3, got 3\n[PASS] Stack Class:              expected stdout 20, got 20\n\n>>> ALL PHASE 3 VERIFICATION TESTS PASSED SUCCESSFULLY! 100% VERIFIED. <<<\n```\n\n---\n\n### Next Phase Readiness\n\n- **Phase 1 (Interface)**: Completed.\n- **Phase 2 (Teaching Substeps)**: Completed.\n- **Phase 3 (Meaningful Animations)**: Completed.\n- Ready to proceed with **Phase 4 — Add interactive learning** (optional learner prediction prompts before selected steps: \"What will `c` become?\", \"Will this condition be True or False?\", with answer reveal and explanations).","truncated_fields":["content"]}
